            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner (John D. Cline) argues that Congress placed the phrase \u201cwith respect to its stock\u201d in \u00a7301(a) to limit the application of \u00a7301(c) to corporate payments made in a non\u2011shareholder capacity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-809007d149a7-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-809007d149a7-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government argues that a controlling shareholder cannot embezzle from his corporation and that, under Ninth Circuit precedent, a defendant must show objective intent to make a distribution with respect to stock before a return\u2011of\u2011capital defense can be presented."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-809007d149a7-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court requires factual evidence of three elements: a distribution with respect to stock, the corporation\u2019s lack of earnings and profits, and the defendant\u2019s sufficient basis in the stock to cover the funds received."
      }
    ],
